 "notes": "Km 0 is the départ réel on the D1091 north of Le Bourg-d'Oisans, 1.3 km before the Rochetaillée turn onto the D526 (after the neutralised start in Le Bourg-d'Oisans, not included). Its position is not published as a coordinate; it was placed 8.4 routed km before the official 'Le Verney/Vaujany' timetable point (taken as the junction of the Vaujany road at the Verney dam), which then also matches Le Rivier d'Allemond at 15.1 (routed 6.72 km for an official 6.7). Official km used as anchors (cyclingstage/letour timetable, ledicodutour, dhnet): Le Verney 8.4, Le Rivier d'Allemond 15.1, Col de la Croix de Fer 33.7, intermediate sprint Saint-Julien-Mont-Denis 66.5, Saint-Michel-de-Maurienne 75.6 (foot of the Télégraphe), Col du Télégraphe 87.6, Les Verneys 95.1, Col du Galibier 110.5, Col du Lautaret 119.0, La Grave 129.4, Mizoën 144.4, Col de Sarenne 156.5, finish 170.9; every anchor-to-anchor stretch routes within ±3 % on the Overture road graph, other km are interpolated from routed distances. Timetable points that were checked but not anchored: Les Oulles 60.4 and Saint-Jean-de-Maurienne 61.6 (route reaches the D926 entry to Saint-Jean, Avenue Samuel Pasquier, at ~62.0), Valloire 91.1 (= Les Granges, the first houses of Valloire; the centre on Avenue de la Vallée d'Or is at ~93.0). Route (ledicodutour locality list, hedgehogcycling, bikeradar, isere.gouv): D1091 → D526 at Rochetaillée (Pont Rouge), Route de Savoie, Route des Fonderies Royales below Allemond and the hairpins to the Eau d'Olle viaduct, Le Verney, Articol, Le Rivier d'Allemond, Barrage de Grand'Maison, Combe d'Olle (D926 in Savoie), junction below the Col du Glandon, Col de la Croix de Fer; D926 via Saint-Sorlin-d'Arves, Les Chambons, Pont d'Entraigues, the Arvan gorge (Viaduc des Sallanches), Charvin/La Combe Bérard/Le Crêt/La Bettaz hairpins, Pierre-Pin, into Saint-Jean-de-Maurienne (Av. Samuel Pasquier, Av. des Clapeys, Av. du Mont Cenis, Rue du Parc de la Vanoise, Av. du 8 Mai 1945); D1006 via Villard-Clément, Saint-Julien-Mont-Denis, Les Oeillettes to Saint-Michel; D902 (Rue du Galibier) over the Télégraphe, Les Granges, Valloire, Les Verneys, Bonnenuit, Plan Lachat to the Galibier summit road (not the tunnel; the summit point is on the col road above the tunnel, so the two summit-loop points must be kept), descent to the Lautaret; D1091 via Villar-d'Arêne, La Grave and the Grand Tunnel du Chambon to the D1091/D25 junction; D25 via Mizoën, Route du Ferrand, Clavans-le-Bas, Clavans-le-Haut, then the narrow Sarenne road (hairpins) to the Col de Sarenne and down the Sarenne valley to the Altiport; through the resort and down the Route d'Huez to the D211 hairpin above Huez, then up the D211 Route de l'Alpe (last ~3.3 km, final hairpins) to the finish on Avenue du Rif Nel. Low confidence: (1) the resort section Altiport → Avenue des Marmottes → Rond-Point de l'Europe → Avenue de Brandes → Chemin de la Chapelle → Vieil Alpe → Route d'Huez → D211 (km ~164–167.6): bikeradar describes the race going down towards Huez and back up the last hairpins of the classic climb, but the exact streets are not published; the 'Huez/hairpin 3' seed km 167.2 and a '4 km' final climb do not exactly match this junction (3.3 km before the line); (2) the intermediate-sprint coordinate is placed at the official km 66.5 on the D1006 (Villard-Clément), not at a published line position; (3) the foot of the Croix de Fer (km 9.7) is placed by the official climb length; (4) Barrage de Grand'Maison and Combe d'Olle valley points are positioned from the DEM profile, and the D526/D926 department border is approximate. The Col de la Croix de Fer (2066 m), Télégraphe (1566–1570 m), Galibier (2640 m) and Sarenne (1987–1991 m) points were checked against Copernicus GLO-30. Points named after a road with '(near X)' were added along the routed race road to keep spacing and to stop the router using parallel shortcuts (Route du Village in Allemond, Chemin des Choseaux at Saint-Sorlin, Route des Seignes on the Télégraphe, the Fontcouverte back roads above the Arvan gorge, the Galibier tunnel).",
